  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656306",
      "title": "An Important Note about Route Observables",
      "lectureOrder": 460,
      "videoOrder": 422,
      "sourceHash": "bba6b0204dcd623fadfbd5fe0c04b93846712b800379f693b6889e18ba6cf71f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we learned how we can subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "to our params to update them or to react to any changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "to them and update our page if we already are on that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "And we set up this subscription using observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "and this works fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "and you don't have to change anything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "I want to bring something to your attention though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "The fact that you don't have to add anything else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "to this component here, simply is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 30.3,
          "en": "because Angler does something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 32.7,
          "en": "for you in the background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 34.8,
          "en": "which is super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 37.95,
          "en": "It cleans up the subscription you set up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.95,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "whenever this component is destroyed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "Because if it wouldn't do this, what are you doing here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "You're subscribing to parameter changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "and let's say you then leave this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "and later you come back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "Well, once you left, this component will be destroyed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.26,
          "en": "and when you come back, a new one will be created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.26,
          "end": 58.98,
          "en": "But this subscription here will always live on in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.98,
          "end": 61.59,
          "en": "because it's not closely tied to your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "So if the component is destroyed, the subscription won't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 69.36,
          "en": "Now it will be here because Angler handles this destroying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.36,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "of the subscription for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.88,
          "en": "But theoretically, you might want to implement the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.88,
          "end": 79.88,
          "en": "OnDestroy Lifecycle Hook, importing it from at Angler Core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 82.203,
          "en": "Therefore you have to implement ngOnDestroy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 86.28,
          "en": "And then you could store this subscription here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.28,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "in some property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 91.8,
          "en": "Let's name it params Subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.8,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "which will be of type subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "And subscription needs to be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 101.13,
          "en": "from RXJS subscription, RXJS is the package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.13,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "offering all this observables functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "As I mentioned, it's not shipping with Angler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 109.77000000000001,
          "en": "but Angler is using this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.77000000000001,
          "end": 111.90299999999999,
          "en": "So this type here, this subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.90299999999999,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "this param subscription property is now bound",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "to this subscription we're setting up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "when calling Subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 121.38,
          "en": "This returns as the subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 124.14,
          "en": "And once the component gets destroyed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.14,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "we could now access the subscription and unsubscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "And again, because it's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.01,
          "en": "you don't have to do this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.01,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "you can leave it as it was before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "Because Angler will do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 137.46,
          "en": "for you regarding these route observables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "But if you add your own observables, and I will come back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "to this in the observable section following this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "you have to unsubscribe on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "And I just wanted to bring it to your attention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "because it's always super important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 151.82999999999998,
          "en": "what's happening behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 151.82999999999998,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "Again, it's not necessary here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 156.45,
          "en": "but it doesn't hurt to also do it manually to here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 160.233,
          "en": "It won't add anything bad to your app by doing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
